msync alert_fd: a thread's exit closes its msync alert index as if it were a file descriptor.
For ntdll of the CrossOver 26.3 engine SWTOR on Mac uses (athei's wine-build cx-26.3.0-8, Wine
11.0, dlls/ntdll/unix). Part of SWTOR on Mac, https://github.com/jdrly/swtor-on-mac.

CodeWeavers' msync port onto Wine 11's in-process synchronization (all CrossOver 26.0-26.3
sources) keeps, with msync, the msync shared-memory index of a thread's alert object in
ntdll_thread_data's alert_fd (get_inproc_alert_fd in sync.c). pthread_exit_wrapper then
close()s alert_fd unconditionally, so every thread that ever did an alertable in-process wait
closes an unrelated file descriptor with that number when it exits: a file, another thread's
wineserver pipe ("wine client error"), or a kqueue (lost wakeups). With msync the alert object
belongs to the server and there is no descriptor to close. The same guard as athei/wine
12927acab0 (its arm64 branch), written again for these sources. Found and tested with
SWTOR on Mac's repros (thread churn with alertable waits: EBADF and hangs without it, none with
it); only pthread_exit_wrapper changes.

This patch changes Wine's ntdll, which is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License
2.1 or later (see the copyright headers of the files it changes); the patch and the ntdll.so
built with it are under the same license. Changed by Jan Drlý, 2026-10. Applies to the sources
that engine is built from (CodeWeavers' CrossOver 26.3 with athei's patches):
  https://github.com/athei/wine/tree/d23b39774528237cafe49f9a073286f854b779c0
  (athei/wine@cx-26-patched, named in the release notes of athei/wine-build cx-26.3.0-8)
Built by scripts/build-ntdll.sh.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/thread.c
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 #include "wine/server.h"
 #include "wine/debug.h"
 #include "unix_private.h"
+#include "msync.h"
 
 WINE_DEFAULT_DEBUG_CHANNEL(thread);
 WINE_DECLARE_DEBUG_CHANNEL(seh);
@@ -1104,7 +1105,9 @@
  */
 static DECLSPEC_NORETURN void pthread_exit_wrapper( int status )
 {
-    close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->alert_fd );
+    /* with msync, alert_fd is the msync shared-memory index of the thread's alert object
+     * (get_inproc_alert_fd), not a file descriptor; the server owns that object */
+    if (!do_msync()) close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->alert_fd );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->wait_fd[0] );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->wait_fd[1] );
     close( ntdll_get_thread_data()->reply_fd );
